From: Raphael Linux bring-up <raphael-linux@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: raphael: use normal display handoff and USB peripheral mode

The continuous-splash opt-in assumes the Android XBL display state remains
valid.  In the verified U-Boot -> GRUB path it led to a black panel and a
disp_snapshot NULL dereference.  Let DRM perform a normal modeset instead;
remaining startup SMMU warnings are tracked separately.

The legacy Qualcomm DWC3 wrapper takes dr_mode from the child while the DWC3
core also consumes it.  Pin both nodes to peripheral mode and remove the role
switch so configfs can bind the gadget UDC deterministically.

This is the source-level equivalent of tools/raphael/prepare_runtime_dtb.sh.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
@@ -653 +652,0 @@
-	qcom,boot-display-on;
@@ -1296,0 +1296 @@
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
@@ -1302 +1302 @@
-	usb-role-switch;
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
@@ -1344 +1343,0 @@
-	qcom,boot-display-on;
